infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One composite vs two single-column indexes
  desc Pick by the dominant query's filter shape, not by the schema
  compares
    - label One composite (a, b)
      children
        - label One physical structure
          desc Single B-tree, one write per insert
        - label ~30-50% larger than (a) alone
          desc Storage and write overhead vs a lone (a)
        - label Serves (a) and (a, b) prefixes
          desc Leading-prefix queries narrow on the same tree
        - label Wins when the dominant query always filters by the leading column
          desc Design the composite for that query first
    - label Two single-column (a) + (b)
      children
        - label Two separate structures
          desc Two writes per insert, two trees to maintain
        - label Roughly the sum of both sizes
          desc Size and write overhead of (a) plus (b)
        - label Combined via Bitmap And
          desc Planner intersects two Bitmap Index Scans
        - label Wins when a-alone and b-alone are both hot, never together
          desc No single composite order serves both filters
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
